---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site";
---

<Base title="Download" description="Download Bazza for Windows (CPU or NVIDIA CUDA) and macOS (Apple Silicon or Intel). Free, open-source, offline meeting recorder with local AI transcription and summaries.">
  <section style="padding: 56px 0 24px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
    <h1>Get Bazza {SITE.version}</h1>
    <p class="muted">This local development fork has no public installers or automatic update channel.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="max-width: 640px; font-size: 18px;">Build Bazza locally for your machine. CPU, CUDA and Metal variants use the same features.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Windows, NVIDIA GPU</h3>
      <p class="muted">Uses CUDA for fast transcription and summaries: an 88-minute call is fully processed in about 10 minutes. Needs a GeForce GTX 10-series or newer with 6 GB+ VRAM and a recent driver; nothing else to install.</p>
      <p class="muted">Local build only.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Windows, any PC</h3>
      <p class="muted">Runs on the CPU. Works on any 64-bit Windows 10/11 machine with 8 GB of RAM and an AVX2 CPU (2013 or newer). Slower, but fully featured; Bazza sizes the models to your machine so long calls still finish in reasonable time.</p>
      <p class="muted">Local build only.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>macOS, Apple Silicon</h3>
      <p class="muted">M1 or later, uses Metal. System-audio capture needs macOS 14.6+; older versions record the mic only.</p>
      <p class="muted">Local build only.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>macOS, Intel</h3>
      <p class="muted">For Intel Macs on macOS 13 or later. CPU inference; the CPU tiers of models are selected automatically.</p>
      <p class="muted">Local build only.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section style="margin-top: 56px; max-width: 720px;">
    <h2>After installing</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="line-height: 1.8;">
      <li>Open Bazza. It checks your mic and system audio, then suggests model sizes for your hardware.</li>
      <li>Download the models once (from Hugging Face, checksum-verified, 1 to 7 GB depending on tier).</li>
      <li>Join a call. When the popup appears, check the window and audio choice and click <b>Record</b>. Or press <code>Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+R</code> anytime to open the same picker.</li>
      <li>Open the recording from the Library to follow captions and running notes while the call is on.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 40px;">Build locally</h2>
    <p class="muted">From the local repository, install dependencies with <code>pnpm install --frozen-lockfile</code>, prepare native sidecars with <code>node scripts/prepare-bundle.mjs --profile dev</code>, then run <code>pnpm tauri dev</code>. See the repository's development testing guide for toolchain requirements.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
